# TNA Platform — E2E Testing Strategy & Implementation Plan

## Background

The TNA (Total National Address) platform serves 4 distinct user roles (Visitor, Owner, Gov-User, Carrier) across a Next.js App Router architecture with i18n (ar/en), Zustand state management, and mock data layers. The current test infrastructure consists of a single `smoke.spec.ts` with 2 basic assertions. This plan designs a production-grade Playwright E2E suite.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Critical Fix Required**: The TNA issuance detail page (`/gov/tna-queue/[id]`) is **missing entirely** — no `[id]` directory exists under `tna-queue/`. This causes a 404 when Gov users click "Review" on any TNA request. The address-queue detail page (`/gov/address-queue/[id]/page.tsx`) exists and is fully functional — it must be used as the architectural blueprint to reconstruct the TNA detail page.

---

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 1. **Base URL**: Should tests target `localhost:3000` (dev server) or a dedicated test server? Current smoke test assumes `:3000`.
> 2. **Locale priority**: Should E2E tests run in Arabic (`/ar/`) only, English (`/en/`) only, or both? Arabic is the primary market but English validates i18n completeness.
> 3. **CI Integration**: Do you want GitHub Actions / pipeline config included in this plan, or is local-only sufficient for now?

---

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 0 — Critical Fix: TNA Queue Detail Page

#### [NEW] [tna-queue/[id]/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Kimo%20Store/Desktop/project-tna/project-a/frontend/tna-project/src/app/[locale]/gov/tna-queue/[id]/page.tsx)

Reconstruct the missing TNA issuance review page, mirroring the architecture of `address-queue/[id]/page.tsx`:

- Uses `DetailViewLayout` template with sidebar action panel
- Reads `mockGovQueue` by `request_id` param (+ new `mockTNARequestDetails` lookup)
- Sections: Visitor Information, Eligibility Snapshot, Supporting Documents
- Sidebar: Approve/Reject buttons with processing state → success/failure animation
- Security note panel matching address-queue pattern

**New mock data required** in `gov.mock.ts`:
```ts
