### Phase 5 — Three-Pillar Assertion Library

#### [NEW] [tests/e2e/assertions/visual.ts](file:///c:/Users/Kimo%20Store/Desktop/project-tna/project-a/frontend/tna-project/tests/e2e/assertions/)

**Pillar 1 — Visual & UX Integrity:**
```ts
// Reusable assertions that verify design system compliance
async expectSPATIALTheme(page: Page) {
  // Verify CSS variables are loaded (--color-primary: #2196C9)
  // Verify font-family includes 'Rubik' or 'IBM Plex Sans Arabic'
  // Verify no raw browser-default fonts
  // Verify primary gradient exists on CTA buttons
}
async expectRTLLayout(page: Page) {
  // Verify dir="rtl" on root when locale=ar
  // Verify logical CSS properties (margin-inline, padding-inline)
}
```

**Pillar 2 — Functional Correctness:**
```ts
async expectStateTransition(page: Page, from: string, to: string) {
  // Verify status badge changes from `from` to `to`
  // Verify localStorage/Zustand state reflects change
}
async expectGuardrail(page: Page, errorMessage: string) {
  // Verify error toast/dialog appears with specific message
  // Verify destructive action was blocked
}
```

**Pillar 3 — Flow Continuity:**
```ts
async expectFlowCompletion(page: Page, finalElement: string) {
  // Verify the journey reached the terminal success/failure dialog
  // Verify no intermediate 404s or blank states
  // Screenshot on success for audit trail
}
```

